Third-party material

The app icon is licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; see assets/app-icon/LICENSE.txt. Other original
interface artwork was supplied by the project owner. The offline icon catalog contains Lucide, Feather, Phosphor and
Material Symbols artwork. Their ISC, MIT and Apache-2.0 licence texts are preserved in
assets/icon-packs/LICENSE-lucide, LICENSE-feather, LICENSE-phosphor and LICENSE-material.

Agent tool-call glyphs are from Iconoir 7.12.2 (MIT); the bundled SVGs and licence are in
crates/ui-egui/assets/iconoir/. Source: https://github.com/iconoir-icons/iconoir.

Interface icons based on Figma's UI3 kit include work by Figma and Abhimanyu Rana (@planetabhi).
The free Community artwork is licensed CC BY 4.0; source:
https://www.figma.com/community/file/1486123838948777078/ui3-figmas-ui-kit .
The optional icon package also claims MIT: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@ui3/icons .
These notices cover the SVG and JSON artwork in crates/ui-egui/assets/.

The provider marks embedded in crates/ui-egui/src/icons_ui3.rs identify integrations only.
The OpenAI Blossom comes from OpenAI's published brand artwork via
https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OpenAI_logo_2025_(symbol).svg and is subject to
https://openai.com/brand/. The Anthropic and Google Gemini glyphs come from Simple Icons
(https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons, whose repository is CC0; individual marks may
have separate rights). The Kimi Code glyph comes from
https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-code/blob/main/apps/vscode/resources/kimi-icon.svg
(Apache-2.0; LICENSE-APACHE). The names and marks remain their owners' trademarks.

The cursor images in crates/ui-egui/assets/cursors/ were supplied from an owner reference;
their redistribution licence has not been verified. Confirm rights before distributing them.

Release builds made with the optional craft-fonts build input (CRAFT_FONTS_DIR) embed fonts
including Inter under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each package must carry its font licences.

The Lizard interface embeds NV Legible Next Regular and Bold, adapted by Nico Verbruggen
from Atkinson Hyperlegible Next. The font is distributed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1;
see ATTRIBUTION.md and assets/fonts/nv-legible-next/OFL.txt. Document fonts remain user-selected.

Rust crate dependencies keep their own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, OFL for egui's
default fonts, CDLA-Permissive-2.0 for the root certificate list webpki-roots compiles in, and
similar permissive licenses); see each crate's metadata.

macOS agent runtime
-------------------
The macOS app bundle includes Node.js 22.23.4 and npm from https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.23.4/
to run provider-supplied agent helpers. Release packaging verifies the pinned SHA-256 digests
before signing. The original Node.js and bundled dependency licences are included at
Lizard.app/Contents/Resources/Licenses/Node-LICENSE and in the bundled npm package.

Language flag icons
-------------------
The rounded PNG flags in crates/ui-egui/assets/language-flags/ come from
open-assets-hub/country-flag-collection (https://github.com/open-assets-hub/country-flag-collection).
Its SVG sources come from lipis/flag-icons (https://github.com/lipis/flag-icons).
Both are distributed under the MIT License; copies are kept beside the PNGs.

Linux Wayland window decorations
-------------------------------
sctk-adwaita 0.10.1 (https://github.com/PolyMeilex/sctk-adwaita,
commit d5f343c45c04d4a026db57f76760819b7325db00) is used by winit on Linux
for vector window controls. Its title-font features are disabled: no Cantarell
font is embedded by this dependency and no font file is added to this repo.

